<title>MONGOLIA: Mongolia gold output falls 46 pct in Jan-April.</title>
<headline>Mongolia gold output falls 46 pct in Jan-April.</headline>
<dateline>ULAN BATOR 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mongolian gold production in January-April fell 46 percent to 117.4 kg from 215.8 kg in the same period last year, the State Statistical Bulletin said in a report seen on Friday.</p>
<p>Mongolia's total gold production was 5,242.1 kg for all of 1996. Most of the gold was mined in the summer and early autumn.</p>
<p>The bulletin gave no further details.</p>
</text>
